# Agent Governance Audit Command

When the user says **"run agent governance audit"**, **"agent governance audit"**, or **"run ai governance audit"**:

## What to do

1. Launch one subagent (generalPurpose) and instruct it to follow `docs/process/agent-governance-audit-process.md`.
2. Require output report at `docs/audits/agent-governance/YYYY-MM-DD-agent-governance-audit.md`.
3. Audit only. Do not make code changes.
4. Require the audit to explicitly check:
   - hook-vs-doc and rule-vs-doc drift
   - where recurring guidance should live (hook vs rule vs process doc vs setup doc)
   - workflow consistency between hooks, rules, audit docs, and day-to-day PM/builder usage
5. After completion, summarize top findings and report location.

## References

- Process: `docs/process/agent-governance-audit-process.md`
- Reports: `docs/audits/agent-governance/`
